        <body>
            <div xml:id="d487">

                <pb facs="0848" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg752"/>

                <head>No. 485.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 22, 1874</date>.
                        (Received July 7.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 159.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a note from Mr.
                    Lafragua, minister of foreign affairs, dated May 27 last, making inquiry, in
                    view of the facts referred to in said note, if this legation has taken any
                    resolution on the subject of displaying its flag on the days of Mexican
                    anniversaries. A similar note was also addressed to all the foreign legations in
                    this capital. I replied to Mr. Lafragua, under date of the 29th ultimo,
                    (inclosure 2,) that this legation had taken no new resolution upon the subject,
                    and stated to him what had been its practice in relation thereto.</p>
                <p>I have received no reply to my note, but I have reason to believe that my answer
                    has proven satisfactory to the Mexican government, which has manifested a
                    sensitive regard for the observance of its national anniversaries.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN W. FOSTER.</signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d487-a1.xml" xpointer="d487-a1"/>
